matched_variant_raw.rewritten_question_text:
According to the measurement results over several years of rainfall and biomass at several trophic levels in the ecosystem (shown in the figure below), if the rainfall is 120 inches, please infer what the biomass range of the primary consumers is?

\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
 xlabel=Rainfall (inches),
 ylabel=Biomass,
 xmin=0, xmax=140,
 ymin=0, ymax=250,
 xtick={0,20,...,140},
 ytick={0,50,...,250},
 legend pos=north west,
 ymajorgrids=true,
 grid style=dashed,
]

\addplot[
 color=blue,
 mark=square,
 ]
 coordinates {
 (20,200)(40,150)(60,100)(80,50)(100,25)(120,10)
 };
 \addlegendentry{Producers}

\addplot[
 color=red,
 mark=triangle,
 ]
 coordinates {
 (20,60)(40,120)(60,180)(80,240)(100,180)(120,150)
 };
 \addlegendentry{Primary consumers}

\addplot[
 color=orange,
 mark=o,
 ]
 coordinates {
 (20,10)(40,20)(60,30)(80,40)(100,50)(120,45)
 };
 \addlegendentry{Secondary consumers}

\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}

